  "passage": "A museum displayed ancient glass bottles in blue, green, and brown. Students were surprised that glassmaking was so old.\nThe guide explained that glass required heat, materials, and skill. Some bottles held perfume, medicine, or oil. Others showed wealth and trade.\nStudents compared them with modern plastic bottles. Glass was heavier and breakable, but it could last for centuries.\nThe exhibit made students think about materials differently.\nPlastic feels convenient because it is light and cheap. Ancient glass reminds us that durability can outlive its owners. Every material carries a future after use.",
